<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guangxi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guangxi is an autonomous region of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, with Nanning as its capital. Its karst landscape around Guilin is famous, and it is home to the Zhuang, China's largest ethnic minority. Long a frontier of the Chinese empires, it was ruled by the Southern Han in the 10th century, and in 1851 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiping-rebellion">Taiping Rebellion</a> began there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guangxi.jpg" alt="Guangxi" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: chensiyuan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1_li_jiang_guilin_yangshuo_2011.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
